# Cloudflare Workers static-asset headers (plan Task 8, spike G09).
#
# WHY THIS FILE EXISTS: with the `cloudflare-module` preset, prerendered routes
# (`/`, `/en`, the marketing pages, `/blogs` index…) and everything under
# `/_nuxt/` are served by the Workers *Assets* layer, which never reaches the
# Nitro handler. `routeRules` headers — and therefore `nuxt-security` — do not
# apply to those responses. Measured on `wrangler dev` before this file existed:
# `GET /` returned only `cache-control`/`content-type`/`etag` (no HSTS, no
# `nosniff`, no fake `Server`) and `/_nuxt/<entry>.js` returned the default
# `max-age=0, must-revalidate` instead of the immutable policy the route rule
# declares. Those are exactly the responses a browser hits first, so the gap is
# not cosmetic: HSTS cannot be delivered by a `<meta>` tag.
#
# `nuxt-security` still owns the *rendered* responses (the CSP is injected as a
# `<meta http-equiv>` into prerendered HTML and as a response header for SSR),
# and this file deliberately does not add a second `Content-Security-Policy`:
# two policies intersect, so the app stays the single authority for CSP.
#
# Cloudflare parses this file instead of serving it, and it is only consumed by
# the Workers assets runtime (Vercel ignores it; the file is inert there).

/*
  Strict-Transport-Security: max-age=63072000; includeSubDomains; preload
  X-Content-Type-Options: nosniff
  X-Frame-Options: DENY
  X-XSS-Protection: 1; mode=block
  Referrer-Policy: strict-origin-when-cross-origin
  Permissions-Policy: geolocation=(), microphone=(), camera=()
  X-Powered-By: PHP/5.2.17
  Server: Apache/2.2.15

# Hashed build assets: the `/_nuxt/**` route rule declares this, but that rule is
# only reachable through the Nitro handler — which these URLs never touch.
/_nuxt/*
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=31536000, immutable

/fonts/*
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=31536000, immutable
